CSS FILTERS (FANCY VISUAL EFFECTS)
=================================

CSS filters are used to apply visual effects
to images, backgrounds, or elements
without editing the image file.

They are mostly used for:
- Image effects
- Hover effects
- UI polish
- Modern design visuals


BASIC SYNTAX
------------

filter: filter-function(value);

Example:
filter: blur(5px);


COMMON CSS FILTERS
==================

1. BLUR
-------

Adds a blur effect to the element.

filter: blur(5px);

Effect:
- Makes image or content look out of focus
- Used for backgrounds, modals


2. BRIGHTNESS
-------------

Controls how bright the element looks.

filter: brightness(150%);

Values:
- 100% → normal
- >100% → brighter
- <100% → darker


3. CONTRAST
-----------

Controls difference between light and dark.

filter: contrast(120%);

Higher value:
- Sharper image
Lower value:
- Flat look


4. GRAYSCALE
------------

Converts image to black and white.

filter: grayscale(100%);

Values:
- 0% → normal color
- 100% → fully grayscale

Common use:
- Hover effects


5. SEPIA
--------

Adds a brown / old-photo look.

filter: sepia(100%);

Used for:
- Vintage effects
- Artistic images


6. SATURATE
-----------

Controls color intensity.

filter: saturate(200%);

Values:
- 100% → normal
- >100% → more colorful
- <100% → dull colors


7. INVERT
---------

Inverts the colors.

filter: invert(100%);

Effect:
- White becomes black
- Black becomes white

Used for:
- Dark mode tricks
- Creative effects


8. OPACITY
----------

Controls transparency.

filter: opacity(50%);

Note:
This is different from opacity property
because filter affects only visuals.


9. HUE-ROTATE
-------------

Rotates the color wheel.

filter: hue-rotate(90deg);

Effect:
- Changes colors dramatically
- Fun, fancy UI effects


COMBINING MULTIPLE FILTERS
==========================

You can apply multiple filters together.

Example:
filter: grayscale(100%) blur(2px) brightness(120%);

Order matters:
Filters are applied from left to right.


HOVER EFFECT EXAMPLE (COMMON USE)
================================

Normal:
filter: grayscale(100%);

On hover:
filter: grayscale(0%);

Used for:
- Image galleries
- Portfolio websites


IMPORTANT NOTES
===============

- Filters do NOT affect layout
- Filters are visual only
- Too many filters can hurt performance
- Mostly used on images and backgrounds


INTERVIEW WORDING
=================

"CSS filters allow applying visual effects
such as blur, brightness, contrast, and color
adjustments directly using CSS, without
modifying the original image."


WHEN TO USE FILTERS
===================

- Image hover effects
- Background blur
- Modern UI polish
- Creative visuals

WHEN NOT TO USE
===============

- Heavy animations
- Large images on low-end devices
